# #1143: SPY0335 is the uniform answer for an uncalled generic reference, whatever the callee kind.
# The bare-identifier and user-instance arms are pinned by generic_function_reference_uncalled_1138,
# the BCL arm by bcl_generic_instance_method_uncalled_1136, the .NET-module arm by the Stdlib
# json_loads_uncalled_reference fixture, and the user-module arm by
# usermod_generic_func_uncalled_reference_1142. The BUILTIN arm is the one that had unit coverage
# only: map[int, int] matches the two-type-parameter overload, so the #1004 arity check passes and
# the reference resolves — leaving SPY0335 as the only thing between it and codegen.
def main() -> None:
    f = map[int, int]
